//
Day 98 – Aggregation Pipeline

Task:
Use $match, $group
👉 Build:
Count users


Like SQL:

GROUP BY
COUNT()
SUM()
AVG()

MongoDB equivalent:

$match
$group


Aggregation Syntax
db.collection.aggregate([
   { stage1 },
   { stage2 }
])


1. $match

Used to filter documents.

Example:

Find only CSE students.

db.users.aggregate([
  {
    $match: { branch: "CSE" }
  }
])


or 
db.users.aggregate([{$match : {branch : "cse"}}])


2. $group

Used to group documents.

Example:
Count total users.

db.users.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: null,
      totalUsers: { $sum: 1 }
    }
  }
])


Group by Branch

Count users branch-wise.

db.users.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$branch",
      total: { $sum: 1 }
    }
  }
])


MATCH & GROUP
db.users.aggregate(
  [
    {
     $match : {branch : "CSE"}
    },
    {
      $group: {_id : null, totalUsers: {$sum : 1}}
    }
  ]
)